ection" :answer-field/id #uuid "062dbebe-305a-56c5-8611-abf6286429e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104122/selection/ebeacfc20214c23623b19938e5c955b942cb857a8998a2c19ef8ac3bf49b4233" :answer-field/choices ["q-104122/selection/0f532246fc1de001b0911fadf788b921521602a4be3c16fa56ceb4e65fad1cea" "q-104122/selection/38a3973a725911bee55c7fff1ce41bb39a5665f04b910a6df41c8392ce097011" "q-104122/selection/ebeacfc20214c23623b19938e5c955b942cb857a8998a2c19ef8ac3bf49b4233" "q-104122/selection/ec40a961885c25250d2a173dfb0b6f0f1659ea17b862cb6ddd85301b1e2a18e8" "q-104122/selection/75240c0806d09a4baff9e6c1200561057a90b44d8af6a2f2b5bf16dc0d98a012"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104122" :question/id #uuid "8fdc10d8-c29b-5c00-b56a-60501ddc763f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104122" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}}=2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{-4}.\n$$\n\nDe Moivre's Theorem states that\n\n$$\n[\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\phi +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\phi ]^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-4$ and $\\phi =2\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{4}} & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2\\theta ]^{-4} \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-4)\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(-4)\\theta )] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta )].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-8\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-8\\theta )]=2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8\\theta )].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104122/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ed5facf-f654-5890-974f-bbdcd9641515"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104122"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325342/field-1/099b5cd50267aa764e684c36b8c8c10a9defc031691acd691dbaee08ca05917f" :answer/id #uuid "5e5da26f-240a-54bd-b79e-44d9e8706d90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(5\\theta)+i\\sin(5\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325342/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "13b7f863-d13f-535d-8b3a-ecde08437ddd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325342/field-1/099b5cd50267aa764e684c36b8c8c10a9defc031691acd691dbaee08ca05917f" :answer-field/choices ["q-325342/field-1/099b5cd50267aa764e684c36b8c8c10a9defc031691acd691dbaee08ca05917f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325342" :question/id #uuid "10a59e4f-3a26-5fd9-ab1c-381e84f0a8da" :question/math-academy-id "q-325342" :question/problem "Express $\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{5}}$ in the form $x+\\text{i}y,$ where $x$ and $y$ are functions of $\\theta .$ Use $i$ to denote the imaginary unit.\n\n$\\frac{1}{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]^{5}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{5}} & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor expressions involving subtraction, De Moivre's theorem states that\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )]}^{n}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\phi )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\phi ).\n$$\n\nIn our expression, we have $n=-5$ and $\\phi =\\theta .$ Substituting in these values, we get\n\n$$\n{[\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )]}^{-5}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\theta )\n$$\n\nFinally, using the fact that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\phi )=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\phi )$ and $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\phi )=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\phi )$ for any input $\\phi ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-5\\theta )-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-5\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )-[-\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta )] \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5\\theta )+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325342/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc91582-8d44-5de1-9c98-1c5de173eefb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325342"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325338/field-1/85eaba0b93b2b2b52bff45fb320cb9b093a6e4fd21f63c27ddde7db254e54fce" :answer/id #uuid "260b5115-43d1-55de-b863-0549df326153" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(48\\theta)-i\\sin(48\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325338/field-1/d61c1050fe1576fa901b728a8c7d68962da88c2fed4b243b49226d3c09cd1295" :answer/id #uuid "25a0ea42-3625-50cb-b7d4-519f82ca192a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\cos(48\\theta)+i\\sin(48\\theta)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325338/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ae2578d-56ad-567e-bbce-d0cfa0cbaf71" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325338/field-1/85eaba0b93b2b2b52bff45fb320cb9b093a6e4fd21f63c27ddde7db254e54fce" :answer-field/choices ["q-325338/field-1/85eaba0b93b2b2b52bff45fb3